{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01SMSFusga9xauK8EtjCmt91","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n\n## Project State Analysis\n\n### Problem\ngo-unix-utils is a specification-driven development experiment that re-implements classic Unix utilities in Go. Formal specifications are derived from C source code, Go implementations are generated from those specs using an AI coding agent (mage-claude-orchestrator), and correctness is verified through differential testing against Homebrew GNU reference binaries.\n\n### Architecture\n- **cmd/**: Per-utility Go packages (ts, cat, wc, sponge, ls, du)\n- **pkg/testutils/**: Differential testing harness comparing Go vs GNU reference binaries\n- **pkg/sys/**: Darwin/Linux syscall abstractions (terminal width, file metadata, signals)\n- **pkg/format/**: Shared output formatting (columns, ANSI color, human-readable sizes)\n- **magefiles/**: Build targets bridging human spec work and automated synthesis\n- **docs/**: Specifications (PRDs, use cases, test suites, roadmap)\n\n### Current Implementation State\n- **pkg/testutils**: Code exists (`difftest.go`, `normalize.go`) — harness operational\n- **cmd/ts**: Code exists (`main.go`, `ts_test.go`) — implementation and differential tests present\n- **cmd/cat**: Code exists (`main.go`) — implementation present, **no test file exists yet**\n- **cmd/wc**: No code yet (PRD complete, use case/test suite written)\n- **cmd/sponge**: No code yet (PRD complete, use case/test suite written)\n- **pkg/sys**: No code yet (PRD complete)\n- **pkg/format**: No code yet (PRD complete)\n\n### Current Release\n**rel01.0** (in_progress): ts specification and differential test — ts appears to have implementation and tests. The use case `rel01.0-uc001-ts` is `in_progress`.\n\n**rel01.1** (pending): wc, cat, sponge — PRDs complete, use cases and test suites written. cat has implementation but no tests. wc and sponge have no code.\n\n### Priority Reasoning\n\nrel01.0 has ts implemented with differential tests. The next priority is rel01.1 which covers wc, cat, and sponge. These three utilities share only pkg/testutils (already implemented) and require no pkg/sys or pkg/format.\n\ncat already has `cmd/cat/main.go` but has **no test file**. Per the dependency ordering and the test suite `test-rel01.1.yaml`, the next task should be creating the differential tests for cat. This is the highest-priority gap: implementation exists without verification.\n\nwc and sponge have no implementation code yet. Per canonical ordering (implementation before tests, but cat already has implementation), the cat tests come first since they unblock verification of an already-implemented utility.\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"cmd/cat differential tests (prd006-cat R1-R5, prd001-testutils R1-R3)\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - cmd/cat/main.go (existing cat implementation to understand flag handling and output behavior)\n      - pkg/testutils/difftest.go (DiffTest struct, RunDiffTests API, FileExpectation)\n      - pkg/testutils/normalize.go (NormalizeFunc, ComposeNormalizers, TimestampNormalizer as reference pattern)\n      - cmd/ts/ts_test.go (reference for how to structure differential tests -- TestMain build pattern, baseEnv, test case layout)\n      - docs/specs/product-requirements/prd006-cat.yaml (all requirements R1-R5 and acceptance criteria)\n      - docs/specs/test-suites/test-rel01.1.yaml (test case definitions for cat: cat_default_passthrough through cat_missing_file)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/cat/cat_test.go\n        action: create\n        note: Differential tests for cmd/cat exercising all cat test cases from test-rel01.1.yaml\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Create a TestMain function that builds the Go cat binary into a temp directory and locates the Homebrew reference binary gcat via exec.LookPath(\\\"gcat\\\"). Follow the same pattern as cmd/ts/ts_test.go TestMain. Clean up the temp directory after tests complete.\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Define a baseEnv variable set to []string{\\\"LC_ALL=C\\\"} per test-rel01.1.yaml preconditions. All test cases must use this environment to eliminate locale-dependent divergence.\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Implement test case cat_default_passthrough: no flags, file input passes through verbatim. Create a temp file with known content \\\"hello\\\\nworld\\\\n\\\", pass the file path as args. Verify stdout matches byte-for-byte with no normalization. Traces prd006-cat R1.1, R1.5.\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"Implement test case cat_binary_passthrough: no flags, stdin contains all 256 byte values (0x00-0xFF). Verify output bytes are identical to input bytes with no normalization. Traces prd006-cat R1.4.\"\n      - id: R5\n        text: \"Implement test case cat_line_numbering_n: -n flag with stdin \\\"alpha\\\\n\\\\nbeta\\\\n\\\". No normalization. Traces prd006-cat R2.1.\"\n      - id: R6\n        text: \"Implement test case cat_line_numbering_b: -b flag with stdin \\\"first\\\\n\\\\n\\\\nsecond\\\\n\\\". No normalization. Traces prd006-cat R2.2, R2.4.\"\n      - id: R7\n        text: \"Implement test case cat_squeeze_blanks: -s flag with stdin \\\"a\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n\\\\nb\\\\n\\\". No normalization. Traces prd006-cat R3.1.\"\n      - id: R8\n        text: \"Implement test case cat_show_nonprinting: -v flag with stdin containing bytes 0x01, 0x09, 0x1b, 0x7f, 0x80, 0xff. No normalization. Verify caret and M- notation matches gcat -v. Traces prd006-cat R4.1, R4.2.\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Follow the cmd/ts/ts_test.go pattern exactly: TestMain builds the binary, sets goBinary and refBinary package-level vars, a single TestCatDifferential function defines a []testutils.DiffTest slice and calls testutils.RunDiffTests(t, goBinary, refBinary, tests).\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"For test cases that require file fixtures (cat_default_passthrough, cat_multiple_files, cat_missing_file), create the fixture files inside the test function using t.TempDir() and os.WriteFile. Set the DiffTest.WorkDir to the temp directory and use relative file paths in Args.\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"For cat_binary_passthrough, construct the 256-byte stdin slice programmatically in a loop (for i := 0; i < 256; i++ { ... }) rather than embedding a literal.\"\n      - id: D4\n        text: \"The reference binary is gcat (Homebrew coreutils), not cat (macOS BSD). Use exec.LookPath(\\\"gcat\\\") to locate it. Skip tests if gcat is not found.\"\n      - id: D5\n        text: \"No normalization is needed for any cat test case. Cat output is deterministic -- there are no timestamps or non-deterministic fields. All DiffTest.Normalize fields should be nil.\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"cmd/cat/cat_test.go exists and compiles without errors.\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"go test ./cmd/cat/... runs without build errors when goBinary builds successfully.\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"All 14 test cases from test-rel01.1.yaml cat section are present as DiffTest entries: cat_default_passthrough, cat_binary_passthrough, cat_line_numbering_n, cat_line_numbering_b, cat_squeeze_blanks, cat_show_nonprinting, cat_show_ends, cat_show_tabs, cat_show_all, cat_flag_e, cat_flag_t, cat_flag_u_accepted, cat_combined_ns, cat_multiple_files, cat_stdin_dash, cat_missing_file.\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"Each DiffTest entry has a Name matching the test case name from test-rel01.1.yaml.\"\n      - id: AC5\n        text: \"Each DiffTest entry has a comment referencing the traces from test-rel01.1.yaml (e.g., '// Traces: prd006-cat R1.1, R1.5').\"\n      - id: AC6\n        text: \"File fixture test cases (cat_default_passthrough, cat_multiple_files, cat_missing_file) create fixture files in t.TempDir() and set WorkDir on the DiffTest.\"\n      - id: AC7\n        text: \"The test file follows the copyright header and package declaration pattern from cmd/ts/ts_test.go.\"\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":90867,"cache_read_input_tokens":18565,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":90867},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0df5cbaa-ead6-422b-9328-49c2a0ef44eb","uuid":"2e3a33b0-280a-46df-b01f-fa982386d71f"}
